# Generated benchmark output. Keep the directory (via .gitkeep) but do not commit
# results by default; force-add a specific report if you want to publish findings.
*
!.gitkeep
!.gitignore

# Published snapshots are committed, but only their report artifacts are
# re-included. A blanket `!snapshot/**` would also cancel the root .gitignore
# rules for this subtree (.env.*, *.pem, *.key, *.log, __pycache__, ...), so a
# stray secret or generated file in a snapshot would be staged by default.
#
# The artifact allowlist below must be extended in lockstep when the published
# names or set change (BENCH_CSV, BENCH_REPORT and the report/chart formats);
# anything outside it deliberately stays ignored, so a missing file in
# `git status` means the allowlist is stale rather than the file being lost.
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/benchmark.csv
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/dataset.txt
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/hardware.txt
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/postgres-settings.txt
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/report.md
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/**/report-*.svg
!lhorner_laptop_oct_2026/strategy-comparison.md
